# Add native dig:// protocol support for the DIG Browser.
#
# Registers the dig:// URL scheme and resolves dig://<urn> resources END-TO-END,
# natively, following the SAME contract as the reference dig-chrome-extension
# and the ecosystem SYSTEM.md ("JSON-RPC 2.0 read methods", "Retrieval key",
# "Merkle inclusion proof", "AES-256-GCM-SIV + HKDF-SHA256"):
#
#   * parse the URN (full urn:dig:<chain>:<storeID>[:<root>]/<resourceKey> form
#     and the dig:// shorthand, with optional ?salt=<hex> for private stores);
#   * retrieval_key = SHA-256(canonical rootless URN) (net/url_request/dig_crypto.cc,
#     content ADDRESSING only — not the read-crypto);
#   * POST JSON-RPC 2.0 dig.getContent to an EXTERNAL dig-node over the §5.3 ladder
#     (dig_url_loader_factory.cc; 3 MiB streaming windows);
#   * verify the Merkle inclusion proof against the chain-anchored root, then
#     derive the per-URN AES-256 key and AES-256-GCM-SIV-decrypt — ALL via the
#     digstore-core Rust read-crypto, called DIRECTLY through the dig_runtime FFI
#     (dig_read_verify_decrypt; chrome/browser/dig/dig_native_runtime.cc);
#   * render the verified + decrypted bytes (fail-closed on any tamper/decoy).
#
# There is ONE trustless read-crypto impl in the ecosystem — the digstore-core
# Rust. The native browser links + calls it via FFI; webpages (extension/hub/SDK)
# use the SAME Rust through its dig-client-wasm binding. WASM is for webpages only;
# the browser carries NO native C++ verify/decrypt (#44 SoC; @mt-dev ruling).

